<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christian the Younger of Brunswick</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1599–1626</span> · Also known as Christian of Brunswick</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christian the Younger of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> was a German Protestant commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War and administrator of the prince-bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halberstadt">Halberstadt</a> from 1616. Champion of the exiled Elizabeth Stuart, he raised armies for the Palatine cause, but was defeated at Höchst in 1622 and Stadtlohn in 1623. He died of illness in 1626.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christian-the-younger-of-brunswick.jpg" alt="Christian the Younger of Brunswick" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anthonie van Ravesteyn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Herzog_Christian_von_Braunschweig-L%C3%BCneburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
